collector
---------

collector is a browser-based evidence collection tool for web applications.

Its purpose is to observe web applications as a browser would, collect
structured evidence about what it encounters, and preserve that evidence for
downstream analysis.

collector intentionally separates collection from analysis.  It does not attempt
to identify technologies, infer business logic, detect vulnerabilities or
generate reports.  Instead, it produces a deterministic, versioned dataset that
can be processed by other tools.

Using browser automation together with an HTTP proxy, collector records browser
actions, downloaded artifacts and network traffic while exploring an
application.  The resulting evidence is designed to support workflows such as
application mapping, technology fingerprinting, JavaScript analysis, entity
extraction, AI-assisted reasoning and security research.

collector is built around a small set of focused modules that communicate
through explicit, structured data.  Every stage of the collection process is
intended to be observable, reproducible and independently testable.

See documents in the docs/ directory for more details.
